==Enemy==
Bore is essentially a stronger [[One Horn]], having far higher speed, health and range with a rapid attack cycle, though he is somewhat hindered by having one additional knockback.

==Strategy==
Bore pushes very easily, so a strong frontline is necessary. Using three or four meatshields to stall him is recommended, but they alone won't work without [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red units]] who inflict status effects. These include but are not limited to: [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Pirate Cat]] for knockback, [[Witch Cat (Rare Cat)|Witch Cat]] for slowing, [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Apple Cat]] or [[Evil Cat (Rare Cat)|Evil Cat]] for freezing and [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sushi Cat]] for weakening, as well as also being able to protect other units with its high health. His low range in particular makes him vulnerable to iCat and [[Goggles Cat (Special Cat)|Goggles Cat]], who can outrange and completely paralyze him. DPS units can then move in and tear him up before he starts causing trouble again.

Fighting Bore without [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-controllers]] is possible. Anti-Red attackers such as [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]], [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Whale Cat]], [[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Dark Lazer]] and [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] can all be used to great effect, preferably with [[Cat Combo]]s to increase their stats like [[Brave Cutter (Combo)|Brave Cutter]], [[Cool Japan (Combo)|Cool Japan]], [[Seasons of Love (Combo)|Seasons of Love]] or [[Three Kings (Combo)|Three Kings]]. Provided your cats are sufficiently leveled and Bore isn't too buffed, these units will quickly diminish his health down to nothing. That being said, brute force becomes less and less effective in later Bore appearances, where his magnification can reach or exceed 400%, dealing too much damage for said attackers to handle.

