==Variants==
{{Variant
|original = Bore
|Nimoy Bore
|[[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] variant of Bore. Inferior speed, attack rate and base health but has a 50% chance to knockback [[Cat Units]].
|Boraphim
|[[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] variant of Bore. Much stronger and moves significantly faster, but has 5 knockbacks as opposed to the usual 2 on most others.
|Razorback
|[[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] variant of Bore. Has extremely high health, speed and DPS, while strengthening by 50% at 50% health.
|Dread Bore
|[[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] variant of Bore. Stats are similar to Bore's except for speed, which is slightly lower than Boraphim's. It has a long burrow distance among Zombies, and revives once with 50% HP.
|Li'l Bore
|A much smaller and weaker variant of Bore found in [[Year's First Dawn|You Nears! 2019]], [[Year's End Event#Most Appearances 2020|Most Appearances 2020]] and [[Infernal Tower]] Can be easily defeated.
|Bore Jr.
|[[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] variant of Bore. Relatively fragile, but deals extremely high damage and creates Lv.5 [[Mini-Wave]]s with his attacks.
|Mystery Snowmound
|A snow-covered Razorback introduced in [[Snow Doges]]. Has one more frame of backswing compared to Razorback, but is otherwise identical.
}}

